Yes, GOhA are selbri. Using go'i in a tanru does the same as any other=20
tanru, in this case the following happens:

A: xu do se bangu lo lojbo
B: go'i milxe

Here "go'i" stands for "se bangu be fa mi bei lo lojbo be'o" and thus=20
the tanru is "se bangu be fa mi bei lo lojbo be'o milxe", which you=20
could expand to "milxe lo ka se bangu lo lojbo", the mi in milxe1 is=20
implicit.


